WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.000
Your key numbers deserve the spotlight.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.133
In this lesson, you will learn to show measures in card visuals, copy and

3
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:12.167
line them up quickly, and add clear titles with text boxes.

4
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:14.000
Let's make your page shine!

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.809
Here is our Product table:

6
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:20.100
twenty two products, in three categories.

7
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.856
On the report page, a card shows one big number.

8
00:00:40.856 --> 00:00:43.620
This one shows Number of Products: twenty two.

9
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.118
I create a second measure, Number of Category, with COUNT on the Category column,

10
00:00:58.118 --> 00:01:00.140
and show it in another card.

11
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.108
Quick trick:

12
00:01:14.108 --> 00:01:19.767
select a visual, press Control C and Control V, then drag the new field into it.

13
00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.951
Keep cards the same size and line them up.

14
00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:24.720
A tidy page builds trust!

15
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.838
Now, a text box.

16
00:01:52.838 --> 00:01:58.588
On the Insert tab, click Text box, and type a short title, like Count or DistinctCount.

17
00:01:58.588 --> 00:02:02.900
Use the font, size, and bold buttons to make it stand out.

18
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.977
Titles tell readers what each group of numbers means.

19
00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:36.940
Here, the first row shows COUNT results, and the second row will show DISTINCTCOUNT results.

20
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.440
Next, I start the measure Number of Products Remove Duplicates, with DISTINCTCOUNT.

21
00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.540
Your page is taking shape!

